<Legal
  title="Terms of Service | Adelaide Airport to Barossa"
  description="The terms for Adelaide Airport to Barossa transfers: flat fares from $200, vehicles and drivers, waiting time, luggage, booster seats and cancellations."
  slug="terms"
  h1="Terms of Service"
  updated="3 August 2026"
>
  <p>These terms apply to transfers and day tours booked through
    adelaideairporttobarossa.com.au. By lodging a booking request you agree to them.</p>

  <h2>Requests and confirmations</h2>
  <p>Submitting the form on this site is a <strong>request</strong>, not a confirmed booking, and no
    payment is taken at that point. Your booking exists once we reply in writing with a flat fare
    and pick-up details and you accept it.</p>

  <h2>Fares</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Fares are quoted as one flat price per car, each way, unless we say otherwise in writing.
      The price is per vehicle, not per passenger, and is the same in either direction.</li>
    <li>Our published transfer fares between Adelaide Airport and the Barossa Valley are
      <strong>$200</strong> for a sedan (up to 4 passengers), <strong>$230</strong> for the Tarago
      people mover (up to 7 passengers) and <strong>$250</strong> for the HiAce commuter bus (up to
      13 passengers).</li>
    <li>Those fares apply to the <strong>central Barossa townships</strong>: Tanunda, Lyndoch,
      Nuriootpa, Greenock and Angaston. Transfers to townships outside that central area may be
      quoted at a higher price, which we will confirm in writing before you book.</li>
    <li>Cellar-door day tours and vehicle hire by the hour or day are quoted separately on
      enquiry.</li>
    <li>The fare we confirm in writing is the price you pay. There is no meter and no surge.</li>
    <li>Any fare estimator on this site is indicative only. The written quote is what counts.</li>
    <li>Extra stops, extra waiting time or a changed destination on the day may change the price;
      we will tell you before the extra cost is incurred wherever we can.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Vehicles and drivers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All of our drivers are fully accredited in line with the South Australian government
      regulations that apply to passenger transport vehicles.</li>
    <li>All vehicles have passed the South Australian Government mechanical inspection required for
      passenger transport, and are air-conditioned, non-smoking and cleaned inside and out.</li>
    <li>We will send a vehicle appropriate to the passenger and luggage numbers you give us when
      you book. We reserve the right to substitute a comparable or larger vehicle from our fleet at
      no extra cost to you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No payment is taken when you lodge a request. Payment is arranged once we have confirmed
      your flat fare in writing.</li>
    <li>We accept Visa and Mastercard, bank transfer, and cash to the driver on the day.</li>
    <li>Regular and corporate clients can be invoiced by arrangement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Flights, delays and waiting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give us your flight number and we track it, so your driver adjusts to the real landing time
      at no extra cost to you.</li>
    <li>If you cannot find your driver, call <a href="tel:+61447958346">0447 958 346</a> before
      leaving the terminal.</li>
    <li>If you do not arrive and do not contact us, the booking is treated as a no-show.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">[FREE WAITING TIME AND WAITING FEES — owner to confirm, e.g. 60 minutes free
    after landing, then a per-hour charge.]</p>

  <h2>Cancellations and changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cancel more than 48 hours before the scheduled pick-up time and no charge applies.</li>
    <li>Cancel within 48 hours of the scheduled pick-up time and a cancellation fee may apply. We
      will tell you the amount before it is charged.</li>
    <li>If nobody arrives at the pick-up point and we are not contacted, the booking is treated as
      a no-show.</li>
    <li>Changes to the date, time or destination are subject to availability. Tell us as early as
      you can and we will move the booking rather than cancel it wherever we can.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Passengers, luggage and booster seats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Tell us passenger numbers and any oversized luggage when you book, so we send the right
      vehicle. We cannot carry more passengers or luggage than the vehicle is licensed for.</li>
    <li>Child booster seats are available on request. Tell us the ages of the children when you
      book so the right seat is fitted before pick-up.</li>
    <li>Seat belts must be worn. Smoking and vaping are not permitted in any vehicle.</li>
    <li>Water and other non-alcoholic drinks may be consumed on board. <strong>Alcohol may not be
      consumed in the vehicle.</strong> Sealed bottles and cases purchased at a cellar door may of
      course be carried.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the cost of cleaning or repair if the vehicle is soiled or damaged
      during your trip.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our liability</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable care to get you to your destination on time, but we are not liable for
    delays caused by traffic, weather, road closures, breakdowns or other events outside our
    control. Our services come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian
    Consumer Law. Nothing in these terms limits those rights.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the law of South Australia.</p>

